# Keep the auto-generated at-rest encryption key out of the build context, so a
# non-default DATABASE_PATH cannot bake one host's secret into the image. The
# same goes for the SQLite database itself and its WAL/SHM sidecars, which sit
# next to that key wherever DATABASE_PATH points (`data` above only covers the
# default), and for stray TLS keys — the set `.gitignore` already ignores.
# `**/` is required: unlike `.gitignore`, a bare pattern here matches the
# context root only, so `.clawstash-key` alone missed `db/.clawstash-key`.
# The final stage copies only the build output (standalone server, static
# assets, `public/`), so this is the backstop for a stray file under `public/`
# and for file tracing pulling the working tree into `.next/standalone` (see
# the `turbopackIgnore` note in src/server/db-access-check.ts).
**/.clawstash-key
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*.sqlite-journal
**/*.pem
**/*.key
*.md
.dockerignore
.gitnexus
.vscode
.idea
coverage
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.claude
agent_docs
